# The build context for packages/dashboard/Dockerfile is this directory — the
# repository root — because the dashboard depends on `@evestack/schedules` over
# the `workspace:*` protocol and only pnpm, running against the root lockfile,
# can resolve that. See the header of packages/dashboard/Dockerfile.
#
# That makes this file load-bearing rather than tidy: without it the daemon is
# handed ~3 GB of node_modules, .next and .git before the first instruction runs.
#
# What must NOT be excluded: pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, and every
# workspace member's package.json. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reads all of
# them to verify the lockfile, so hiding one package's manifest fails the whole
# install with ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE — including packages the dashboard
# never touches.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated on prepack from templates/default; not an input to any build.
packages/create-evestack/template

# eve and Nitro runtime artifacts.
**/.eve
**/.output
**/.nitro

# Secrets. A build context is not a secret store: anything here lands in a layer
# and in `docker history`. The dashboard's credentials arrive as environment at
# run time, never baked in.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# History, CI, and editor/tooling state.
.git
.github
.claude
.vercel
.firecrawl

# Test and QA artifacts. qa-shots alone is 20 MB of screenshots.
**/qa-shots
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report

# Docs site scaffolding — the dashboard build reads none of it.
docs-site

**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
